  "notes": "Traces are polar, relative to menu center. r in density-independent units. thetaDeg uses screen convention where -90 is up. 'expectHighlights' is the edge-triggered sequence of item indices (null = none); 'expectLabels' is the label each highlight effect carried, which must be resolvable without consulting live state. v0.3.0 adds: the outward cancel bound r_cancel = cancelScale * r1, identical in both commit styles; hub-latch highlight suppression; the ring ceiling; prefix-freeness of a chord vocabulary; and the three tempo axes (bpm, div, aps) with their MIDI CC mappings. v0.2.0 added pure suites: quant (quantizeTime), tempo (estimateBpm over 24ppqn ticks, median period), chord (classifyBurst), split (splitBursts). v0.4.0 adds the ring-fit suite: fitRing shrinks r1 toward the band minimum before overflowing a viewport that cannot contain it, and clampRingCentre centres rather than clamping when the viewport is smaller than the ring, because a naive clamp inverts its own bounds and pushes the ring off the opposite edge. Cases may carry a `geom` override; the state machine reads geometry from its own state rather than a module global.",
